    {
      "id": "mechanism",
      "text": "Powerful magnets ride inside the train, and the track walls are lined with coils of wire. As the train speeds past, its magnets make current flow in those coils, so the coils become magnets too. They push the train up and keep it centered. Below 150 kilometers an hour, that current is too weak, so it rolls on rubber wheels.",
